.TH "PB-TEAM-MACHINE-REQUESTS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-machine-requests - List machines waiting for a team owner or admin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team machine requests <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List machines waiting for a team owner or admin

.PP
List machines waiting for a team owner or admin, with who asked and when. Owners and admins see every request; other members see their own, including declined ones.

.PP
A personal machine can be shared with a team while ownership stays personal, or explicitly transferred to team ownership. Sharing and capability grants are separate decisions. Removing a team-owned machine revokes its enrollment; unsharing a personal machine withdraws that team's access.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for requests

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-machine(1)\fP
